m1	680,1450,1305,1570		Two conjunct tetrachords written as note letters joined by dashes, ties marking the semitones: e f g a braced beneath, and a b-flat c d braced above, sharing the common tone a.
m2	672,1680,1305,1795		The changed form: e f g a braced beneath as a tetrachord, a dash to b, and b, a semitone tie, d and e braced above as the trichord (the c is not printed).
